# EcoSort Technical Design

## Architecture

Waste Input → IR/Proximity Sensors → Arduino Controller → Stepper Motor and Servo Gate → Sorting Bins

The analog moisture sensor provides readings to the Arduino. The controller processes the readings and activates the sorting mechanism according to the programmed threshold.

## Pin Connections

| Component | Arduino Pin |
|---|---|
| IR sensor | D5 |
| Proximity sensor | D6 |
| Buzzer | D12 |
| Servo motor | D7 |
| Analog moisture sensor | A0 |
| Stepper motor | D11, D10, D9, D8 |

## Workflow
1. Initialize sensors and motors.
2. Read the proximity sensor.
3. Detect an object using the IR sensor.
4. Read and average three analog sensor values.
5. Compare the calculated value with the threshold.
6. Activate the stepper motor and servo gate according to the condition.
7. Return the mechanism to its initial position.

## Risks and Limitations
- Sensor readings require calibration.
- Waste classification may be inaccurate.
- Motors may jam if the mechanism is poorly aligned.
- Use suitable motor power supplies and test safely.

## Testing
Test each sensor separately, verify motor direction, calibrate thresholds, and record the results before operating the complete system.
